<title>SWEDEN: Astra boosted by takeover rumours.</title>
<headline>Astra boosted by takeover rumours.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rumours about a possible takeover of Swedish drug company Astra boosted the shares in morning trade on Monday to an intra-session record.</p>
<p>At 1110 GMT the share was nine crowns higher at 341 crowns. The share touched an intra session high of 343 crowns earlier in the morning.</p>
<p>&quot;There are still talking about a takeover and it's a stubborn rumour. No trader wants to be short in Astra in this situation,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>On Friday the crown traded nine crowns higher at 336.5 because of a plethora of rumours including Investor selling its Astra stake and links with Swiss rival Roche Holding AG.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
